            "license": "public domain",
            "source_url": "https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Chinese_Classics/Volume_1/The_Doctrine_of_the_Mean",
            "text": "It is said in the Book of Poetry, \"Although the fish sink and lie at the bottom, it is still quite clearly seen.\" Therefore the superior man examines his heart, that there may be nothing wrong there, and that he may have no cause for dissatisfaction with himself. That wherein the superior man cannot be equaled is simply this,-his work which other men cannot see.",
            "translator": "Legge",
            "year": 1885
          }
